To set up a new ACH account for your client and process payments, you'll need to follow these steps:

## Step 1: Create a Processing Account

Send a POST request to the Merchant Platform endpoint with ACH configuration:

**Endpoint:**
- Test: `https://api.uat.payroc.com/v1/merchant-platforms/{merchantPlatformId}/processing-accounts`
- Production: `https://api.payroc.com/v1/merchant-platforms/{merchantPlatformId}/processing-accounts`

Your request body should include ACH-specific details in the `processing.ach` object:

```json
{
  "processing": {
    "ach": {
      "enabled": {
        "isEnabled": true,
        "acquirer": "payroc"
      },
      "amountLimits": 3000,
      "transactionLimits": {
        "max": 10000,
        "daily": 200000,
        "monthly": 6000000
      },
      "acceptCanadianBankAccounts": true,
      "padEnabled": false,
      "secCodes": ["web"]
    }
  },
  "parties": {
    "merchants": [
      {
        "businessDetails": {
          "legalName": "Business Name",
          "addresses": [
            {
              "address": {
                "country": "US"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  }
  // ... other required fields
}
```

## Step 2: Process ACH Payments

Once the account is set up, use the Bank Transfer Payments endpoint:

**Endpoint:**
- Test: `https://api.uat.payroc.com/v1/bank-transfer-payments`
- Production: `https://api.payroc.com/v1/bank-transfer-payments`

**Example request:**

```json
{
  "processingTerminalId": "1234001",
  "order": {
    "amount": 4999,
    "description": "Payment description"
  },
  "paymentMethod": {
    "bankAccount": {
      "routingNumber": "011401533",
      "accountNumber": "1234567890",
      "nameOnAccount": "Account Name",
      "accountType": "checking"
    }
  }
}
```

## Required Headers

For both requests, include:
- `Content-Type: application/json`
- `Authorization: Bearer <token>`
- `Idempotency-Key: <UUID v4>`

